# state: first-run   (recorded on a disk with no save for the title (NOTES.md E); lane.savestate433)
# Shin Megami Tensei: NINE (41540002), Thor. DRAFT by lane.routeprep,
# 2026-09-26, not played. NO FRAMES ON DISK for this title. It was released
# in Japan only, so its menus are in Japanese; every step is [guess].
#
# Aim [guess]: the first item of the title menu (New Game) -> a name-entry
# screen for the protagonist, which in this family usually has a default
# name and a confirm (START) -> the opening scenes in Tokyo. A accepts any
# save-creation prompt. One file: New Game stays the first item, and a later
# run's "load" prompt, if any, is answered the same way.
#
# Adopted by lane.titleroutes 2026-09-30 (session 42) unchanged in its steps
# except where noted, and queued as a Thor screening soak (<= 480 s, the
# fan-dead Thor's cold-slot runner): NOT YET REPLAYED. Every step leaves a
# frame, so a soak that misses gameplay is the survey that revises it.
wait 30
shot boot30
press START                 # [guess] skip logos/FMV
wait 15
shot boot45
press START
wait 15
shot boot60
press START                 # [guess] title prompt
wait 8
shot title-menu             # CHECK: the highlighted item should be the first (new game)
mark booted
press A
wait 8
shot after-new-game         # OPEN: save-slot creation, or the name entry
press A
wait 8
shot name-entry
press START                 # [guess] accept the default name
wait 6
shot name-confirm
press A                     # [guess] confirm YES
wait 10
shot story
repeat 10 {                 # was 12: the heat stop
    press A                 # [guess] advance the opening dialogue
    wait 5
    shot story-a
}
mark gameplay               # [guess] placeholder: move to the first frame with the player moving
repeat forever {
    axis LY min
    wait 2
    axis LY mid
    press A
    wait 1
    axis LX max
    wait 1.5
    axis LX mid
    press A
    wait 1
    axis LX min
    wait 1.5
    axis LX mid
}
